                        Born from the creative synergy of songwriting partners Ed Vallee and Kelly Padrick, "The Stranger I Chose" emerged from the vibrant New York City music scene of the late 1980s.

This evocative composition explores the complex emotional aftermath of a fleeting encounter - where moments of passion give way to creeping regret, gnawing mistrust, and the sting of betrayal. The song masterfully captures the haunting duality of transgressive desire.

Originally recorded in a raw, intimate session at Ed Vallee's home studio (2011), the song has now been reimagined with lush production and the captivating vocals of Paula Clare, breathing new life into this timeless story.
